      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-data-semantic-verification-contract/v1-candidate\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate-construction-only\",\n  \"scope\": \"Add Query and domain Mapping v1/v2 execution to the existing explicit Python semantic verifier. Public-boundary Mapping v3 stays explicitly pending until its Interface-dependent observer is integrated. No source profile or CLI default changes.\",\n  \"reference\": \"Separate target-independent source witness preparation from TypeScript module binding. Both languages reuse the existing checked-source Query evaluator, Mapping evaluator, structural samples, interned recipes, predicate/ordering/limit witnesses and positive/negative expectations. Do not construct a fake TypeScript plan for Python.\",\n  \"native_inputs\": \"Realize shared fact recipes as Python plain dict/list inputs, exact int or canonical decimal strings, explicit None, and native hostile containers/scalars. JavaScript safe-number recipes become exact Python int; unsafe-number controls become rejected Python float. Undefined uses a non-None sentinel. JavaScript-only property/prototype/collection hostile shapes map to rejecting Python subclass/nonstring-key controls; plain frozen/null-prototype records map to ordinary Python data with independent mutation checks. Preserve required/optional absence semantics and do not silently omit any shared case.\",\n  \"native_outputs\": \"Require immutable native fact results, ordered Query row occurrences and declared field projections; compare type-tagged normalized values against shared expectations. Preserve exact arithmetic, UTF16-compatible strings and ordering, identity-sensitive sets, optional values, sum variants, explicit Mapping inputs/defaults and no hidden calculations or factory execution.\",\n  \"observation\": \"Move the existing independent Python Query and Mapping AST observers into compiler-owned sources. Check the exact field model and private planner metadata against authored contracts. Compile in-memory return/effect substitutions with refreshed advertised hashes and require semantic rejection; do not write or execute mutants.\",\n  \"execution\": \"Use the existing exact-source replay and single private native workspace, bounded subprocess, clean environment and final source/toolchain/workspace/cleanup checks. No per-node repository copies or new temporary dependency trees. Retain all source node and formal obligations; partial executed semantics never imply complete verification.\",\n  \"bounds\": \"Retain the shared reference capacity limits and global Python case/byte bounds. Capacity failures remain explicit and cannot drop source nodes or become passes. Bounded cases are not universal proofs.\"\n}\n",
