      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-factory-semantic-verification-contract/v1-candidate\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate-construction-only\",\n  \"scope\": \"Execute checked Entity and Value Object factories through create, reconstruct, Entity transition and declared extension chains. Reuse the shared source lifecycle requests and independent whole-source owned observer without changing generated runtimes.\",\n  \"reference\": \"Preserve every shared lifecycle request, Rule failure, validator order, invalid previous/fields precedence, identity-change result, optional omission, extension failure and exhaustive bounded extension permutation. Bind validator traces to current source closures and actual Python module hashes. Unsatisfied witnesses or case/chain capacity keep the whole factory not_evaluable, not a passing subset.\",\n  \"representation\": \"Compare semantic views, trace outcomes and native/source key equivalence classes, not TypeScript-specific metadata or key bytes. Python snapshots, fields, results, traces, validators, collections, factories and extension tuples retain their native immutable/nominal contracts. Entity equality uses identity, Value Object equality uses all fields. JS frozen and null-prototype field inputs transport as exact inert Python dictionaries, not a promise to accept mapping subclasses; accessor/non-enumerable/inherited negatives transport as hostile subclasses and must not be accessed.\",\n  \"execution\": \"Check fresh snapshots and factory extensions, unchanged inputs/previous snapshots/base factories, stable keys and equal hashes, no source identity collapse or splitting, foreign/clone rejection, constructor guards and exact native errors. Compile and reject two independent return/effect substitutions for each factory. Reuse the pinned owned recipe runtime for nested values and factory construction witnesses.\",\n  \"integration\": \"Preserve single-workspace and bounded-stdin execution, total case/byte/process limits and final source/toolchain/workspace/cleanup invalidation. Keep all other metatypes and formal/cross-generator obligations explicit. No public CLI default, database operation, product policy, admission or release changes.\",\n  \"claim_ceiling\": \"Bounded source-directed native lifecycle verification, not universal proof, arbitrary Python isolation, external persistence or full CLI completion. Native exception shields retain prior generator regression evidence; source-pure Rules cannot manufacture ambient exceptions.\"\n}\n",
