      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-interface-semantic-verification/v1-candidate\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"scope\": \"Source-bound native Python Interface verification in the reconciled project verifier\",\n  \"meaning\": [\n    \"Reuse complete source-derived public and endpoint protocol cases, qualified identity keys and exact/backward consumer-version cases without building a TypeScript project.\",\n    \"Bind registered native module metadata to the same source graph, Interface contract and checked field compilation; retain no duplicate generated artifacts.\",\n    \"Independently observe the complete selected Interface Python grammar, structural input/output types, asynchronous callable member signatures, public aliases, version policy and only declared shared-runtime imports.\",\n    \"Execute every ready case against imported generated Python boundaries; compare normalized values and keys, repeatability, frozen detached output, unchanged input and zero input coercion or observed effects.\",\n    \"Normalize public domain values structurally. Do not execute their factory invariants, Interface members, transport or transactions.\",\n    \"Preserve source distinctions: lists are ordered, sets are canonical and unique, public contracts and named domain values retain qualified identity, UInt64 remains exact, and absent optional values remain explicit.\",\n    \"Check three immutable bindings and two compiling source substitutions for each Interface. Whole-workspace custody and prerequisite invalidation remain owned by the enclosing verifier.\"\n  ],\n  \"capacity\": {\n    \"per_node_cases\": 4096,\n    \"per_node_control_bytes\": 8388608,\n    \"overflow\": \"whole row not_evaluable; never certify a passing prefix\",\n    \"transport\": \"unchanged bounded stdin and existing isolated Python process\"\n  },\n  \"claim_ceiling\": \"Finite source cases and recognition of the selected generated grammar, not arbitrary Python equivalence, a hostile-code sandbox, full CLI qualification, profile activation, product approval or release.\"\n}\n",
