      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-owned-observation-contract/v1-candidate\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate-construction-only\",\n  \"scope\": \"Independent complete native source observation for payload sums and their Entity/Value Object factory dependencies. Required by semantic verification; source observation does not discharge pending sum/factory behavioral execution.\",\n  \"inputs\": \"Use the registered plan's checked field model, source-selected factory bindings, private factory/Rule metadata and source Rule contracts. Retain metadata only, never child artifact arrays or copied emitted source as the expected result.\",\n  \"observation\": \"Recognize the finite generated Python grammar independently of emitters: exact scalar/named/optional/list/set/inline-sum protocols and annotations, owned imports and nominal case classes, complete sum assembly, factory fields and identity, Rule bindings and argument paths, ordered validators and extensions, reference annotations and metadata, constructors and module effects. Observe every selected declaration and transitive Rule; pin shared values, factories and references runtime source bytes.\",\n  \"meaning\": \"Preserve Entity identity versus complete Value Object equality, checked optional/list/set field wrappers and declared reference projection metadata. Reference bindings do not import target factories, dereference records or prove target existence. No new profile or runtime behavior is introduced.\",\n  \"sensitivity\": \"Independent tests must reject compiling changes to owned protocols, identity, validators, dependency modules, constructors, reference annotations, extensions and extra statements, plus checked binding metadata and shared runtime corruption. Exercise nested inline sums, named sums, records, plain Enums, Rule fact conversions and relocated output.\",\n  \"integration\": \"Run in the existing semantic verification process and single bounded workspace, compare exact observed coverage, retain prior native/semantic rows, source/toolchain checks and final failure invalidation. Existing 30-second process and 8MiB controls bounds remain in force. Pass pinned program plus controls through stdin with a 10MiB total bound and a small isolated Python launcher, avoiding the per-argument argv limit without writing another script file. Prior source capsule assets remain unchanged.\",\n  \"claim_ceiling\": \"This observer establishes complete selected native source shape and dependency binding for the bounded candidate, not universal equivalence, arbitrary-Python safety, factory lifecycle execution, full CLI completion, approval or release. Remaining execution and formal obligations stay explicit.\"\n}\n",
