      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-project-planning-contract/v1-candidate\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate-construction-only\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"selection\": \"Explicit Python profile, module root, existing layout and authored field/factory/Operation/Workflow bindings. No caller artifacts, executable callbacks or revived checked snapshots.\",\n  \"meaning\": \"All thirteen reconciled metatypes lower through their Python adapters from one registered whole-project graph. Existing field, boundary, action, Workflow and public contract checkers retain semantic authority.\",\n  \"numeric\": \"Native exact UInt64 integers with the already selected Python adapter input normalization and checked arithmetic. No TypeScript numeric profile or legacy number lowering is implied.\",\n  \"composition\": \"Merge identical shared artifacts only, reject conflicting definitions, resolve Python module and symbol imports, preserve required package initializers, and require native realization coverage for every graph node. Selected node artifacts are an import-closure projection of the whole checked plan, never an independent partial compilation.\",\n  \"sources\": \"Use the compiler-bundled domain contracts, exact Python strict profile and reference-factory contract. Preserve all predecessor capsule bytes. Bind selected source identities into the plan; do not read mutable development files during generation.\",\n  \"evidence\": \"Native AST/import and positive/hostile behavior are required separately from deterministic planning. A registered plan is not proof of semantic qualification or release readiness.\",\n  \"staging\": \"This candidate implements the whole-project generator join. Cross-project composition adapters, existing public source/snapshot/node/project/build command wiring, application output and verification must be completed before R10 qualification; unsupported staged paths fail explicitly, never silently fall back.\",\n  \"effects\": \"Planning and artifact selection are non-effectful. No native process, filesystem publication, provider execution, admission, activation or default CLI cutover.\"\n}\n",
