      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-semantic-verification-contract/v1-candidate\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate-construction-only\",\n  \"inputs\": \"Use registered Python graph/plan and private compiler-retained Calculation metadata. No serialized metadata may revive registration. Retain all source node obligations, including not-yet-implemented semantic executors.\",\n  \"execution\": \"Explicit semantic verification reuses the native verifier's exact-source replay, single private workspace, selected interpreter, bounded subprocess and final currentness/cleanup checks. It calls only source-bound generated pure Calculations in this slice; no Operation/provider side effects are requested.\",\n  \"calculation\": \"Use the existing shared independent BigInt AST evaluator for v1/v2 exact arithmetic outcomes. Compare native Python int and canonical decimal string inputs, actual int result or exact TypeError/ValueError code, evaluation order, overflow, underflow, division-by-zero and declared rounding for bounded source-derived vectors. Reject malformed containers, hostile scalar/key subclasses and unselected inputs without coercion. Observe immutable bindings and complete native provider syntax against checked source contracts.\",\n  \"controls\": \"Each selected Calculation must pass the compiler-owned independent AST observer. Compile in-memory provider substitutions with refreshed advertised hashes and require semantic rejection; never write or execute these mutants. The oracle is source arithmetic and native AST observation, not generated descriptors alone.\",\n  \"bounds\": \"At most 4096 cases per Calculation, 65536 total cases and 8MiB of prepared control metadata. Bounds fail closed and do not discard obligations. Arithmetic vectors are bounded differential evidence, not universal behavioral proof.\",\n  \"claims\": \"Calculation observations may pass only after execution and final native prerequisites. Unsupported semantic nodes remain not_evaluable; partial semantic coverage cannot pass selected-generator-semantic-controls. Cross-generator and formal checks remain required. Existing native-only API does not execute domain behavior; public stronger CLI remains unchanged until complete integration.\",\n  \"compatibility\": \"Reuse shared TypeScript arithmetic without changing its expected results, error classification or existing cases. Preserve native-only contract, all thirteen Python metatypes, all thirty-nine language cells, current CLI defaults and the accepted no-Python-endpoint composition scope.\"\n}\n",
