      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"domainspec.python-sum-semantic-verification-contract/v1-candidate\",\n  \"authority_effect\": \"none\",\n  \"status\": \"candidate-construction-only\",\n  \"scope\": \"Execute payload-bearing Python sums, including nested sums, plain Enums, Entity and Value Object dependencies, using the shared checked owned-value context and source case generator. Keep full factory lifecycle and all remaining metatype/formal obligations explicit.\",\n  \"reference\": \"Extract source sum case preparation without changing existing TypeScript cases or reference meaning. Preserve all source recipes, positive views, identity equivalence, negative cases, bounded capacity and whole-row not_evaluable on missing record witnesses. Append every source-predicted dependency factory probe, including rejection traces; never pass a prefix that omits a variant.\",\n  \"native_execution\": \"Use exact scalar types, immutable tuple collections, owned nominal case classes and validated record snapshots. Check source views, fresh equivalent sums, key equivalence classes without collapse/splitting, baseline equality, equal hashes, frozen component bindings, constructor guards, structural clones and foreign reloaded module ownership. Execute record witness creation and check source outcomes plus bound validator traces before using nested values.\",\n  \"representation\": \"Python native keys need not have TypeScript's byte encoding. Compare their one-to-one correspondence with sampled source identity classes. Treat sets as unordered when comparing cross-language views; do not force TypeScript key ordering on Python. Plain native Enum members do not acquire an invented frozen-object guarantee.\",\n  \"negative_transport\": \"Realize every shared negative recipe explicitly, using hostile subclasses for JavaScript accessor/inheritance/array-shape cases, non-string keys for symbols, float for unsafe Number and structural clones for plain Enums. Compare existing Python leaf errors: INVALID_STRING/INVALID_BOOL versus shared INVALID_COMPONENT, INVALID_SUM_PAYLOAD for extra sum fields, and UNOWNED_COMPONENT for owned record/named-sum rejection. Retain shared expected errors beside the exact native mapping; do not mask unknown exceptions or change generated runtime behavior.\",\n  \"integration\": \"Use the existing single bounded workspace and isolated process, bounded stdin transport, final source/toolchain/workspace/cleanup invalidation and existing total case/byte limits. Reuse observed dependencies and prior executors. Compile and reject two in-memory sum return/effect substitutions per executed root. No public CLI default, release or admission changes.\",\n  \"claim_ceiling\": \"These are bounded source-directed semantic cases and dependency factory construction probes, not universal proof, full factory lifecycle completion or full CLI readiness. Retain unsatisfied and capacity-limited sums as explicit not_evaluable rows.\"\n}\n",
